---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About Jo Fernwood"
  description="Jo Fernwood trained as a mechanical engineer and translates German machine documentation into English, and nothing else."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>An engineer who translates</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="lead">
        I’m Jo Fernwood. I trained as a mechanical engineer, and I translate technical documentation
        from German into English for machine builders.
      </p>
      <p>
        I work alone, and I translate only one kind of document: the operating manuals, maintenance
        instructions, specifications and safety notes that go with machines.
      </p>
      <p>
        My engineering training means I read a German manual the way the engineer who wrote it intended.
        I understand what the machine does, so the English describes it correctly, and your own engineers
        spend less time reviewing it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I work with technical writers and documentation managers at small and mid-size machine builders
        in Germany who sell abroad. Each client’s terminology is kept and used on every job, so the same
        parts carry the same names across all their manuals.
      </p>
      <p>
        The service is entirely online. You email the documents; I send back the English.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
